  ("Since H is sound, from A `H (p → r), we have (p → q) ∧ (q → r) |=H (p → r)," 0.2282 0.8729 0.6441 0.6642 0.6613 0.0134 0.0055 0.4529 0.0436)
  ("or ((p → q) ∧ (q → r)) → (p → r) is valid." 0.1812 0.5340 0.6637 0.6833 0.6809 0.0134 0.0054 0.4805 0.0170)
  ("Hilbert system is one of the earliest inference systems and has great impact to" 0.2282 0.8730 0.6872 0.7006 0.7006 0.0134 0.0055 0.3024 0.0595)
  ("the creation of many inference systems. However, theorem proving in this system" 0.1812 0.8730 0.7068 0.7202 0.7202 0.0134 0.0072 0.2643 0.0266)
  ("has always been considered a challenge because of its high complexity. Since Hilbert" 0.1812 0.8729 0.7264 0.7398 0.7398 0.0134 0.0051 0.2898 0.0277)
  ("systems can hardly be a practical tool for problem solving, we state without proof" 0.1812 0.8730 0.7460 0.7594 0.7594 0.0134 0.0066 0.2638 0.0646)
  ("the completeness result of Hilbert system." 0.1812 0.5324 0.7657 0.7791 0.7791 0.0134 0.0064 0.2969 0.0266)
  ("Theorem 3.2.7. The Hilbert system is sound and complete, that is, A |= B iﬀ" 0.1812 0.8729 0.7940 0.8136 0.8113 0.0134 0.0089 0.3118 0.0858)
