  ("(b) (¬(A → B) | α) ` (¬B | α)" 0.5862 0.8547 0.3359 0.3556 0.3532 0.0196 0.0054 0.4098 0.0230)
  ("where α and β, possibly empty, denote the rest formulas in a sequent." 0.1812 0.7675 0.3726 0.3860 0.3860 0.0134 0.0064 0.2710 0.0489)
  ("In natural deduction, a sequent is deduced from a set of axioms by applying" 0.2282 0.8729 0.3922 0.4056 0.4056 0.0134 0.0068 0.2492 0.0175)
  ("inference rules repeatedly. Each sequent is inferred from other sequents on earlier" 0.1812 0.8730 0.4119 0.4253 0.4253 0.0134 0.0071 0.2266 0.0739)
  ("lines in a proof according to inference rules, giving a better approximation to the" 0.1812 0.8730 0.4315 0.4449 0.4449 0.0134 0.0073 0.2301 0.0373)
  ("style of proofs used by mathematicians than Hilbert systems." 0.1812 0.6941 0.4511 0.4645 0.4645 0.0134 0.0064 0.2933 0.0384)
